<<<
dual(istic). Both words are of the learned kind, & better avoided when such ordinary words as two, twofold, twin, double, connected, divided, half- &-half, ambiguous, will do the work:—The skirt was dual (divided), & rather short./Dual (double) ownership./The dual (connected) questions of ‘ abnormal places’ & a minimum wage would bring about a deadlock./
===
**dual(istic).** Both words are of the learned kind, & better avoided when such ordinary words as *two, twofold, twin, double, connected, divided, half-&-half, ambiguous,* will do the work:—*The skirt was dual* (divided), *& rather short./Dual* (double) *ownership./The dual* (connected) *questions of ' abnormal places' & a minimum wage would bring about a deadlock./*
>>>

